#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "The EMIS domain model"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "What an education management information system holds, how it is divided into domains, and the rules every implementation follows when it models them. The capabilities describe the platform; this page describes the data the platform exists for. Code lists and local terms vary by country; the resources and rules below do not. Every term here is defined in the language of its bounded context, listed in the [context map]{1}; how the contexts are designed is in [domain design]{2}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "Domains"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "Each domain is a catalog per environment (`<domain>_<env>`, [CAP-CATALOG.2]{1}) with one owning steward. A resource lives in exactly one domain and is referenced, never copied, by the others. Each domain belongs to one bounded context ([domain design]{2}); a context may own several."
msgstr ""

