#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "The registries of [CAP-MASTERDATA]{1} are split by what they identify: persons in `people`, institutions and sites in `institutions`, posts in `workforce`. A learner, a staff member and a guardian are not separate registries: they are roles a person holds through relationships ([ADR-0010]{2}). `reference` holds the code lists and dictionary of [CAP-REFERENCE]{3}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "Core resources and relationships"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "Every relationship and fact also belongs to an academic period and uses governed code lists; those links are left out of the drawing for clarity."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "Why it is drawn this way"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**One person, many roles.** A person is recorded once whether they are a learner, a guardian or a staff member, and may be all three over a life; the roles are relationships, not separate registries ([ADR-0010]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Institutions occupy sites.** Two institutions can share one site on different shifts, and one institution can operate on several sites, so the link between them is a relationship with dates. Facilities belong to the site; an institution's services are read through its occupancy."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Enrolment and class membership are separate.** A learner is enrolled in one programme and grade, but may be taught in a class that spans grades or take a subject with a higher grade."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**A post is not a person.** Shortages and vacancies are differences between posts and the people posted to them. A posting carries its share of full time, so a teacher shared between two institutions is counted correctly either by heads or by full-time equivalents."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Facts hang off relationships,** so an attendance session or a result is always attributable to an enrolment in a specific period."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "Modelling rules"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Identifiers are opaque and permanent.** They carry no meaning, and a learner keeps one for life ([CAP-MASTERDATA]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Every changing relationship is effective-dated**, with valid-from, valid-to and recorded-at. A correction adds a version; it never edits history ([P18]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Store events and counts; derive every rate.** Attendance rates, ratios and percentages are computed in the semantic layer from counts, never stored on records, because a stored rate cannot be re-aggregated to a different level ([CAP-TRANSFORMATION.5]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Multi-valued attributes are rows.** A list of languages or subjects is a child table with a code-list reference, not a delimited string or an embedded document. Bronze may hold data as received; silver normalises it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Every coded attribute names its code list and version** ([CAP-REFERENCE.1]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Status and reason are separate.** An enrolment has a state (active, suspended, ended) and, when it ends, an exit reason (completed, transferred, left the education system, deceased). Mixing the two makes transfer and dropout indistinguishable."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Repetition and promotion are derived.** They follow from the progression decision and the next period's enrolment, never from a stored flag, so a correction to either is reflected everywhere."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Formats are fixed once,** in the data dictionary, never per system ([CAP-REFERENCE.6]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/README.md
msgid "**Documents are records.** A certificate, plan or medical note attached to a record is stored by content hash, classified at least as high as the record, and follows the record's retention class ([CAP-RECORDS]{1})."
msgstr ""

